CUDA bfloat16 addition keeps its intrinsic: true
HIP bfloat16 addition keeps its native operator: true
CUDA approximate tanh is its intrinsic under fast math, and the library's without it: true
HIP approximate tanh keeps its library function: true
CUDA half unary functions are its intrinsics under fast math, and the precise f32 function of the widened operand narrowed once without it: true
HIP half unary functions are ROCm's half functions under either hip_fast_math: true
HIP f32 and bfloat16 sin and cos render through the NaN-preserving wrappers: true
HIP's NaN-preserving sin and cos wrappers are defined in its builtins table: true
HIP sqrt, rsqrt and fmod render through their wrappers: true
HIP f64 rsqrt renders as ROCm's rsqrt and f64 fmod through its wrapper: true
HIP's sqrt and fmod wrappers are defined in its builtins table: true
CUDA sqrt, rsqrt and fmod keep the library functions, half fmod widened: true
CUDA f32 sin and cos keep the library functions: true
CUDA bfloat16 ReLU keeps NaN-propagating half intrinsic: true
HIP bfloat16 ReLU keeps its float bridge: true
every HIP arithmetic arity narrows fp8 through the guard: true
every CUDA arithmetic arity narrows fp8 through the vendor type: true
both shared dialects preserve operand evaluation contracts: true
HIP blends value selects over auto locals at f16, bf16, f32 and f64: true
HIP keeps fp8's short-circuiting select, and CUDA every precision's: true
the GPU Satur01 blend binds its operand, then keeps the dialect's own test over the local: true
the GPU Where blend binds both arms, then selects between them with the dialect's own ternary: true
CUDA routine names avoid the names nvrtc rejects as a kernel name: true
HIP routine names avoid the names hiprtc rejects as a kernel name: true
every name of the CUDA table is mangled by the CUDA config: true
every name of the HIP table is mangled by the HIP config: true
ordinary CUDA and HIP routine names stay unmangled: true
